> **Appendix 1**\
\
**Acceptance Criteria for Transfer of Title and Operational\
Responsibilities**\
\
The Signatory Parties hereto shall establish a 'Date of Equipment Title\
Transfer' upon successful conclusion of the following occurrences:\
\
1.  EPC(M) has notified Waltkon Energy of the completion of the\
    > Balance-of-Plant and is prepared to complete the final transfer of\
    > title to Waltkon Energy for the balance of plant equipment.\
\
2.  Waltkon Energy, EPC(M) and AET will establish a date certain to\
    > establish the final 'handover' and transfer-of-title to the\
    > installed A2800 A-T-E-C Reformer units.\
\
3.  The Naboomspruit Renewable Fuels Production Facility management and\
    > its operating personnel, along with the EPC(M) engineers, and the\
    > startup team from AET will initiate the 'plant startup process and\
    > procedure' for each of the ten (10) installed A2800 A-T-E-C\
    > Reformer units.\
\
4.  The Naboomspruit Renewable Fuels Production Facility management,\
    > EPC(M) and AET will initiate startup of each installed A2800\
    > A-T-E-C unit and run each unit for a period of not less than\
    > six(6) but not more than twelve (12) hours to establish a 'steady\
    > state of operational production'. Steady state or run rate is\
    > defined as the equipment performance being compliant with the\
    > operating production metrics as defined within the five points of\
    > demarcation for the A2800 A-T-E-C Reformer as stated in this\
    > Agreement.\
\
5.  Upon completion of documented compliance with the operational\
    > metrics as agreed herein, Waltkon Energy and EPC(M) shall execute\
    > a final compliance and sign-off document for the transfer-of-title\
    > to the installed and operationally compliant A2800 A-T-E-C units.\
    > Such sign-off shall not be unreasonably withheld. Operational\
    > responsibilities of the installed and accepted A2800 A-T-E-C\
    > Reformers shall then be considered 'as accepted' by Waltkon\
    > Energy, and moreover Waltkon Energy shall accept exclusive\
    > responsibility for complete operational compliance of the A2800\
    > A-T-E-C Reformer units.\
\
6.  Upon execution of the compliance document as stated in \'a75 above,\
    > final transfer-of-title will be made upon final payment and\
    > bank-cleared funds received from Waltkon Energy by AET.\
\
